configure_integrated.description:
Routes to any Home Assistant-registered conversation agent — the HA Ollama integration, Gemini, OpenAI Conversation, Claude, or any other LLM you have configured under Settings → Devices & Services.

This type is for **Q&A and general knowledge**. Unlike the HA Intent Processor, there is no device-control filter — any non-empty response is accepted. Cloud agents can be placed here without granting them device-control authority.

{priority_info}

configure_local.description:
Routes to Home Assistant's built-in intent processor (`conversation.home_assistant`) for native **device control** — turning lights on or off, setting thermostats, locking doors, etc.

The **Assist Mode** toggle controls what happens when the HA intent processor cannot match a device command: when enabled, unrecognised requests fall through to the next lower-priority agent (such as a cloud LLM), giving you hybrid device-control + Q&A routing.

{priority_info}

